course: dictionary
lesson: 7167
title: Promising to tell the truth
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Perjury is a long word for a serious idea, but the clues around it help. Look at the words near it: court, promise, truth. Together they point to one meaning: lying after you have promised to tell the truth.
explain: Here is the idea in context: «In UK courts people may swear on a holy book or make a non-religious affirmation; lying in court is perjury, a crime.» People make a promise before they speak in court, so a lie at that moment is perjury. The text says it is a crime.
explain: Notice the promise to tell «the whole truth». Leaving out important parts can mislead people too, so the promise covers more than just avoiding false words. To check your meaning, swap "lying in court" for "perjury" in the sentence. It still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Perjury means telling a lie in court after promising to tell the truth.
fact: Perjury is a crime in UK courts.
fact: People can swear on a holy book or make a non-religious affirmation before giving evidence.
fact: Witnesses promise to tell «the whole truth», because leaving out important parts can mislead too.
fact: Perjury can also mean breaking a solemn promise. Phrases: commit perjury, charged with perjury, guilty of perjury.
exercise: A witness who lies in court after promising to tell the truth has committed what? | Trespass | Politeness | *Perjury | Tardiness
exercise: The text says witnesses promise «the whole truth». What does this promise cover? | *Not lying, and not leaving out important parts that could mislead | Speaking as quietly as possible | Only avoiding false words | Only answering the first question
exercise: «Lying in court is perjury, a crime.» Which word tells you perjury is serious? | *Crime | Promise | Lying | Court
test: Priya reads, «He is charged with perjury.» What most likely does charged with perjury mean? | *Accused of lying in court after promising the truth | Asked to swear on a holy book | Found to be a very kind witness | Given a prize for honesty
test: Which sentence uses perjury correctly? | Perjury is a kind of garden flower | The rain was perjury on sports day | The cake was perjury, so we ate it all | *The witness was found guilty of perjury after lying to the court
exam: Which is the best meaning of perjury? | Telling a joke during a school play | *Lying in court after promising to tell the truth | Forgetting the date of a court visit | Being very kind to a witness
